  "notes": "Theatrical emo-rock with marching-band and glam architecture, modelled on the anthem band because that is the half the research pairs with a backbeat class: \"64–120 for the anthems (half-time feel, backbeat on 3)\". `halfTime` is true and the snare is `halftime_3`; the 132–180 punk band is the other class and is named here. The **documented tempo architecture** is the entry's standout fact — the anthem \"starts at 75 BPM and shifts to 194 BPM 'in half-time', i.e. a double-time drum grid felt as a half-time backbeat\" — which is exactly what `halfTime` true at a mode of 75 encodes, and it is why the model is not simply a slow record. Three drum deltas follow: \"kick 1 and 3 under the march\", \"snare on the marching 16ths\" (a 16th snare roll with an even grouping and almost no gaps), and \"timpani/bass-drum for the theatrical fills\", which is the tom/tomLow/crash perc block on a 4-bar schedule. The melody is documented as G4–D6 — \"the widest range in this lane\" — and the \"gang-choir vocals as a chorus instrument\" are the sustained-pad and octave-echo counter. Sections run long: the entry says 4:30–5:15 with multiple parts, which is the extended `sectionBars` and the high `switchUpProb`. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability.",
